    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d78">

                <pb facs="0133" n="61" xml:id="pg61"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 7655/27–28.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                        Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-03-15"><hi rendition="#italic">March 15,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 562.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Supplementing the department’s instruction
                    No. 539, of January 29, 1909,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d78-f1"/> there is inclosed
                    herewith for your information a copy of an instruction this day addressed to the
                    consul general at Shanghai with reference to the so-called De Menil case. The
                    substance of this instruction should be communicated to the Wai-wu-Pu.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d78-a1.xml" xpointer="d78-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
